# Setting Title Automargin

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

Long titles can overlap with the plot area. Set `title.automargin: true` to
have Plotly automatically expand the top margin to accommodate the title.
Set `title.yref: "paper"` to position the title relative to the paper (0–1),
which prevents it from overlapping tick labels.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: Enum.to_list(1..10),
    y: [2, 4, 3, 5, 4, 6, 5, 7, 6, 8],
    mode: "lines"
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(
  title: %{
    text: "This Is a Very Long Title That Might Overlap the Plot Without Automargin",
    automargin: true,
    yref: "paper",
    y: 1.0
  }
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
